# FT0 Chat Widget - LOCAL ENVIRONMENT SETUP
#
# This file is NOT committed to Git (.gitignore protects it)
# 
# ⚠️  KEEP THIS FILE PRIVATE - Contains API keys
#

# ===== REQUIRED: Choose ONE =====
# Option 1: Manifest API (Primary)
MANIFEST_API_KEY=mk-your-key-here

# Option 2: Claude API (Fallback - if Manifest fails)
# CLAUDE_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here

# ===== OPTIONAL: GitHub Authentication =====
# Use this for:
# - Better rate limiting
# - GitHub-specific features
# - Production deployments
#
# Create token at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Steps:
# 1. Go to https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# 2. Token name: "FT0-Widget-Production"
# 3. Expiration: 90 days (or your preference)
# 4. Repository access: "Only select repositories" → select imKrisK-widget
# 5. Permissions: 
#    - Repository permissions:
#      - Contents: Read-only
#      - Metadata: Read-only
#    - (No account permissions needed)
# 6. Click "Generate token"
# 7. Copy the token (starts with ghp_)
# 8. Paste below:
GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_your-personal-access-token-here

# ===== SYSTEM CONFIGURATION =====
NODE_ENV=production

# ===== DEPLOYMENT NOTES =====
# For Cloudflare Pages:
# 1. Add these variables to Cloudflare Environment Variables
# 2. Do NOT commit this file to Git
# 3. Use .env.example for version control instead
#
# For local development:
# 1. This file is .gitignored (safe to keep secrets)
# 2. Restart dev server after changes: npm run dev
# 3. Test with: curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ft0/chat ...
